title: "Universal Lane Transport Theorem: Finite Profiled and Holonomy-Twisted Transport within Stratified Universality for Resolved Representations"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "P."
    given-names: "Komorebi"
version: "1.16.0"
date-released: "2026-08-31"
abstract: >-
  The finite profiled Universal Lane Transport Theorem gives exact analysis,
  synthesis, matrix composition, refinement, support selection, residuals,
  profile-preserving realization, and fold-loss accounting for declared finite
  split lane systems. Its holonomy-twisted extension proves that, over a finite
  connected chart groupoid, complete local matrices form a matrix local system
  and descended morphisms are exactly its compatible sections, equivalently
  the loop-invariant matrices in one base fiber. Monodromy orbits give the
  finest ordinary globally labeled coarsening, pair orbits govern global
  selectors and orbital composition, and cyclic Fourier idempotents descend
  rationally through Ramanujan-sum projectors.
keywords:
  - lane transport
  - address holonomy
  - matrix local system
  - monodromy
  - orbit descent
  - orbital algebra
  - resolved representation
  - packet decomposition
  - refinement
  - cyclotomic projector
